  text: Strong knowledge of all trading cards (sports and gaming), including pricing, grading, condition, and market trends.
  text: Experience buying, selling, or negotiating sports card deals.
  text: Ability to build trust and maintain productive relationships with collectors and dealers.
  text: Willingness and ability to travel regularly, including weekends for card shows.
  text: Strong spreadsheet skills and comfort learning inventory and payment platforms.
  text: Excellent attention to detail, especially when handling money and high-value inventory.
  text: Ability to work independently, prioritize follow-up, and take ownership of a deal from sourcing through reconciliation.
  text: Sound judgment, clear communication, and discretion with sensitive business and payment information.
# What success looks like:
  text: A growing network of reliable sellers and repeat buying opportunities.
  text: Purchases that align with buying criteria, budgets, and margin targets.
  text: Sellers paid accurately and within agreed timelines.
  text: Inventory logged promptly, with complete purchase and cost records.
  text: Physical inventory, digital records, and financial documentation consistently reconciled.
  text: Fewer loose ends and less day-to-day follow-up required from leadership.
